      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Description: The left ventricle is one of the heart''s four chambers,
    known for its thick muscular walls.



    Location: Situated in the heart''s
    lower left portion, it lies just below the left atrium and is separated from
    the right ventricle by the interventricular septum.



    Function: The left
    ventricle''s primary role is to pump oxygen-rich blood received from the left
    atrium into the aorta, which then distributes the blood throughout the body,
    providing essential oxygen and nutrients to the body''s tissues and organs.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
