      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Description: The mitral valve, also known as the bicuspid valve, is one
    of the heart''s four main valves. It is so named because it has two flaps, or
    "cusps," that regulate blood flow.



    Location: Situated between the left
    atrium and the left ventricle of the heart, it ensures the one-way flow of blood
    from the atrium to the ventricle.



    Function: The mitral valve''s primary
    role is to prevent backflow of blood. As the left atrium fills and contracts,
    the valve opens to let blood flow into the left ventricle. Once the atrium has
    emptied, the valve closes to prevent blood from flowing back into the atrium
    from the ventricle.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
