  m_text: 'Description: The epicardium is the outermost layer of the heart wall,
    situated just beneath the parietal layer of the pericardium.



    Composition:
    Primarily made up of connective tissue, it features blood vessels and capillaries.



    Function:
    Serving as a protective barrier, it reduces friction between the heart and adjacent
    structures. It also supplies nutrients to the outer myocardium through its vessels.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
