      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Description: Also commonly known as the Left Anterior Descending Artery
    (LAD), the anterior interventricular artery runs along the anterior interventricular
    sulcus, positioned between the two ventricles of the heart.



    Location:
    It originates from the left coronary artery and descends along the anterior interventricular
    groove towards the apex of the heart.



    Function: The artery provides oxygen-rich
    blood primarily to the anterior wall of the left ventricle and the anterior part
    of the interventricular septum. It''s often termed the "widowmaker" due to the
    significant risk associated with its occlusion.

















'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
