      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Description: Trabeculae carneae are irregular, raised muscular ridges
    present on the internal surface of the heart''s ventricles.


    Location: They
    are predominantly found within the ventricles of the heart, particularly in the
    right and left ventricles.


    Function: These muscular beams play a role in
    the conduction system of the heart, aiding in the uniform contraction of the
    ventricles. They help prevent suction that could occur due to the ventricular
    walls'' flat surface and ensure efficient blood ejection.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
