      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Description: The superior vena cava is one of the major veins that return
    deoxygenated blood from the body back to the heart.



    Location: Situated
    in the upper part of the mediastinum, it collects blood from the upper half of
    the body and channels it into the right atrium.



    Function: Its primary
    function is to transport oxygen-depleted blood from the head, neck, arm, and
    upper chest regions back to the heart, more specifically to the right atrium.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
