  m_text: 'Description: The right pulmonary artery is one of the two branches of
    the pulmonary trunk, responsible for carrying deoxygenated blood from the heart
    to the right lung for oxygenation.



    Location: After originating from the
    pulmonary trunk, it passes underneath the aorta and then extends towards the
    right lung.



    Function: Its primary role is to transport deoxygenated blood
    from the heart to the right lung, where the blood receives oxygen.'
