  m_text: 'Description: The circumflex artery is a branch of the left coronary artery
    that curves around the left side and posterior aspect of the heart.



    Location:
    Originating from the left coronary artery, it wraps around the left atrioventricular
    sulcus, coursing to the posterior side of the heart.



    Function: It primarily
    supplies blood to the left atrium and the posterior and lateral walls of the
    left ventricle. Various smaller branches of the circumflex artery penetrate the
    heart muscle to deliver oxygenated blood to deeper regions.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
