  m_text: 'Description: The aorta is the largest and main artery in the human body,
    originating from the heart and extending down to the abdomen.



    Location:
    It arises from the left ventricle of the heart, arches backward and to the left,
    and descends within the thoracic and abdominal cavities.



    Function: Responsible
    for carrying oxygen-rich blood from the left ventricle and distributing it throughout
    the body via its systemic branches, ensuring every organ and tissue receives
    the necessary oxygen and nutrients.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
